Let me help you then:

Crawl is ruled by randomness - Nethack gives you a fair chance. That  
means in Crawl you can expect to get killed without any chance  
whatsoever to evade it, while if you know what you're doing, you can  
expect to ascend in Nethack. From Turn one.

In Crawl you're never safe, in Nethack you're never safe from your own  
stupidity.

Nethack offers you many different things to do, various ways to apply  
your possessions, beneficial as well as ways to kill yourself, with  
predictable outcome, while Crawl has a straightforward X does Y. It's  
many things to do with relatively few items, versus one thing to do with  
each of a truck load of items. (Nethack suffers a bit on the weapon side  
in that, though; that could use some cutting down.)

